{"c":[{"id":"177848396eca6f4e","sum":"Executor replaces whole fields (caret/selection/append insertion lives in host or extension, outside its undo ledger). Every Ask route asks Jev's per-field scope question (ask.scope) first: wrap a test Jev stand-in with answeringScope (helper/test/builders.ts).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T132116Z-e94ee4791db7e513","text":"The helper executor replaces whole fields; caret/selection/append insertion runs in the host or extension and never enters the executor undo ledger.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T144012Z-e2952279328219e3","text":"Every Ask route asks Jev's per-field scope question (purpose ask.scope) first, so a test Jev stand-in must answer it: wrap it with answeringScope in helper/test/builders.ts, or Asks refuse or ask back.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0ec40e0d5ae540d2","sum":"I3: an Ask never refuses for unclear fields; settled ones fill, unclear ones are asked beside them when <= 8, else left to the user. Chrome AX shows only a closed select's chosen option; --form-window page walks keep no legend or heading but a radio group's.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T144012Z-ef6cc9d6c94c61fb","text":"I3 ruling: an Ask never refuses for unclear fields or a too-long question; Jev's settled fields fill, unclear ones are asked beside them (AskIntent.sure) only when <= 8, else listed as left to the user (AskIntent.unsure).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T162248Z-4dec6eda4a1a65ff","text":"Chrome AX shows a closed select's selected option only, so realfill-asks' default reader desk has no menu options; --form-window page uses the page walks (helper/fixtures/recorded/realfill-pages), which keep no fieldset legend or heading except a radio group's.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
